---
intent: >
  Convert the playbook hub and vault-root CLAUDE.md planning steps from
  canonical-template byte-compare to seed-semantic presence-only checks,
  so provisionBrain can never return `would-overwrite` for either file.
  The Obsidian MCP prescription keeps its existing byte-identity
  idempotency. Tests are rewritten to match the new contract.
---

## Project Structure

All files already exist. Only `index.ts` and `index.test.ts` are modified; nothing is added or removed.

```
src/tools/init/provisionBrain/
├── .aide                 ← (MODIFY: spec already updated by the spec phase — not in this plan's scope, listed for orientation) intent spec governing this module
├── plan.aide             ← (REPLACED) this file — supersedes the completed v1 plan
├── index.ts              ← (MODIFY) orchestrator: provisionBrain(brainPath: string, mcpConfigPath: string) => Promise<InitStep[]>
│                            default export unchanged in signature; internals of
│                            buildPlaybookHubStep and buildVaultClaudeMdStep swap
│                            compareBytes for a presence-only existence check
└── index.test.ts         ← (MODIFY) Vitest suite. Two drift tests rewritten to assert
                             status: "exists" on drift; helper tests unchanged
```

Internal (non-exported) functions in `index.ts` after this change:

- `exists(path: string) => Promise<boolean>` — unchanged helper, now consumed by the two seed-file step builders as their sole idempotency primitive
- `vaultExists(brainPath: string) => Promise<boolean>` — unchanged
- `safeReadFile(path: string) => Promise<string>` — unchanged, still used by `buildObsidianMcpStep`
- `obsidianMcpEntry(brainPath: string) => McpPrescription["entry"]` — unchanged, exported
- `buildVaultStep(brainPath: string) => Promise<InitStep>` — unchanged
- `buildPlaybookHubStep(brainPath: string) => Promise<InitStep>` — **MODIFIED**: body switches from `compareBytes(filePath, PLAYBOOK_HUB_TEMPLATE)` to `exists(filePath)`. Returns `{ status: "exists" }` when the file is present at `join(brainPath, "coding-playbook", "coding-playbook.md")` regardless of bytes on disk; returns `{ status: "would-create", content: PLAYBOOK_HUB_TEMPLATE }` when absent. The `"would-overwrite"` branch is deleted.
- `buildVaultClaudeMdStep(brainPath: string) => Promise<InitStep>` — **MODIFIED**: same shape of change. Presence at `join(brainPath, "CLAUDE.md")` is the sole idempotency signal. The `"would-overwrite"` branch is deleted.
- `buildObsidianMcpStep(brainPath: string, mcpConfigPath: string) => Promise<InitStep>` — **UNCHANGED**. Continues to use `safeReadFile` + JSON parse + args-tail comparison (not `compareBytes`). MCP retains canonical-template idempotency because it IS a tool-owned config value.

Module-scope constants (unchanged):

- `VAULT_DIRS: readonly string[]`
- `PLAYBOOK_HUB_TEMPLATE: string`
- `VAULT_CLAUDE_MD_TEMPLATE: string`

## Prerequisites

- `@/tools/init/shared/compareBytes` must continue to export
  `compareBytes: (filePath: string, canonicalBytes: string) => Promise<"would-create" | "would-skip" | "would-overwrite">`.
  After this plan, `provisionBrain/index.ts` no longer imports it — but the helper itself remains in use by other canonical-template callers (`versions.json`, methodology docs, etc.). Do not delete, rename, or change its signature.
- `@/types` must continue to export `InitStep`, `InitStepStatus`, and `McpPrescription` with their current shapes. No new status variant is introduced by this plan; the existing `"exists"` and `"would-create"` cover the new behavior.

